  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Let's line up what the stock market actually did during every major war of the last century. The pattern is unsettling.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "fire"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Markets",
            "in wartime."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "World War Two is the clearest case. The enormous war spending is what finally pulled America out of the Great Depression.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "big": "WWII",
          "label": "the spending that ended the Depression",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "War mobilizes an entire economy toward furious, around-the-clock production.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-wareconomy",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · war economy"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Through most later conflicts, the broad market dipped on the first shock, then ground steadily higher.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "rows",
          "kicker": "Stocks through conflict",
          "rows": [
            {
              "rank": "1",
              "name": "WWII",
              "value": "UP",
              "note": "ended the Depression",
              "color": "#1f7a3d",
              "bar": 1.0
            },
            {
              "rank": "2",
              "name": "Vietnam",
              "value": "UP",
              "note": "long grind higher",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.7
            },
            {
              "rank": "3",
              "name": "Gulf War",
              "value": "UP",
              "note": "dip, then rally",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.6
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Remember, a stock is just an ownership claim on a business's future profit.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-stockmarket",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · stock market"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And a huge slice of that profit flows to the defense industry, now an eight hundred billion dollar machine.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "building",
          "big": "$800B+",
          "label": "US annual military budget",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That is the military-industrial complex, wired directly into the market.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-mic",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · military–industrial complex"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "We also only ever plot the winners. The markets that were wiped out simply vanish from the chart.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Survivors only",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "x"
          ]
